# Burnable Clearnet Mirror Headers for Cloudflare Pages / Netlify (ADR-004)
#
# OPERATIONAL RULE:
# - Only deploy clearnet mirrors from OUTSIDE Thailand (independent volunteers / diaspora).
# - NEVER deploy from the same account/IP/person that runs the canonical .onion origin.
# - Copy this file into the deployed site root (`dist/site/_headers`) when publishing to
#   Cloudflare Pages or Netlify, and replace the placeholder .onion address below.
# - On Cloudflare, enable ECH (Encrypted Client Hello) in SSL/TLS -> Edge Certificates
#   to resist Thai ISP TLS SNI blocking!

/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data:; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'; object-src 'none'
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  X-Frame-Options: DENY
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=63072000; includeSubDomains
  Permissions-Policy: accelerometer=(), camera=(), geolocation=(), gyroscope=(), magnetometer=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Resource-Policy: same-origin
  # Note: Cloudflare Pages _headers treats :splat literally (unlike _redirects),
  # so point Onion-Location to the canonical v3 onion root for universal compatibility.
  Onion-Location: http://replace-with-56-char-v3-onion-address-examplexxxxxxxxxxxxxx.onion/
